## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design governance across regional, compliance, and velocity constraints, plus concrete artifacts.

## Key Concepts
- Region-aware deployment and multi-cloud governance
- Per-region feature flags and gating criteria
- Auditable decision logs and RACI
- Incident response SLAs and runbooks
- Rollout plan with canaries, flags, and automated checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-risk score for a deployment
function computeRiskScore(changeSet, regions, telemetry) {
  let score = changeSet.size * 2;
  regions.forEach(r => { if (r.hasResidencyConstraint) score += 5; });
  score += telemetry.meanTimeToRecovery > 300 ? 20 : 0;
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate gating criteria stay aligned with compliance changes?
- How would you monitor flag fragmentation across regions and prevent drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```
